From 771c379249a9fa2856a4a5e87dbcaeefed43fe88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barattolo <barattolo@barattolo.store>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] payment window: put the order back in the book, and start the
 time when the seller says where to send the fiat

Patch 0013 canceled an `active` trade whose buyer's time to pay ended with
no fiat sent. The fault is the same as upstream's taker-timeout (the taker
took the order and did not do his part), so the order now ends the same
way: the hold invoice is canceled (the seller's sats come back), the order
is reset to `pending` with the taker's keys cleared and republished, the
maker is told NewOrder and the taker Canceled, and the server hears
expired / payment-window-republished. A taker bond, if any, is released.

The window now starts when the marketplace says so: the server leaves an
order out of its answer (or says null) until the seller has told the buyer
where to send the fiat, and the daemon counts from the moment it receives
the number (`started_at`). An explicit 0 is "no window"; ids still waiting
are asked least-recently-asked first. Rows answered by a 0013 daemon keep
their old start. A row of an order back in the book is forgotten, so the
next take asks again.
